        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Finally, turn uncertainty into questions. Which claims need corroboration? Whose perspective is absent? What related source could challenge this reading? Compare evidence before making a historical claim. Strong analysis does not ask whether a source is simply biased or unbiased. It asks how the source's perspective affects what it can reliably show."
